                                                      Reminders
A reminder is a notification Workfront sends to prompt someone about work that is due, late or needs attention.
1)automatic 2) remainder send there are 2 way is there to send reminder

Difference in one line each
Automatic reminders are one admin setting that covers all tasks and issues.
Reminder notifications are targeted, customizable, and attached to individual objects.Any attached object: projects, timesheets, tasks or issues


Kind 1: automatic reminders

Applies   --> to	All tasks and issues, system-wide
Triggered ---> when	A task or issue is due, late, or near the planned completion date
Sent to --->	The assignee, the assignee’s manager, or the manager of that manager
Who controls it	--->Only a Workfront administrator can turn it on and edit it
Email template	-->Can’t use one


Kind 2 : reminder notifications

Applies to  -->	Only the object it is attached to: a project, timesheet, task or issue
Triggered --> when	Someone attaches it manually to an object
Sent to	---> Stakeholders such as the owner, creator, approver or assignee
Who sets it up	--->An administrator, or a user with a Standard or Plan license and administrative access to Reminder Notifications
Email template -->	The default email or a custom template

create the reminder notification?
This needs an administrator (or a user with administrative access to reminder notifications).

Step	What to do
1	Main Menu > Setup
2	Email > Notifications > Reminder Notifications
3	Click New Reminder Notification
4	Choose the object type (such as project, task, issue or timesheet)
5	Fill in the fields below
6	Click Save

Attach it to an object?
Anyone with Manage access to the object can do this, once the administrator has created the notification.

Step	What to do
1	Open the task, project or issue
2	Click the Edit icon
3	In the left panel, click Settings
4	Under Reminder Notification, select one or more notifications
5	Click Save Changes


